 "about": "English functional place labels for the top-down view (wave G1, item 2.5; written by CAM, drawn by OV in mods/battles_overlay.js). Plain words for viewers who have never heard of Nanjing; the Chinese name goes small under the English in --lang en (zh_hant = Traditional, as all Chinese on screen: tools/nanjing/film/trad.js). Positions are the gazetteer places.json's (same ref), so status/src are the gazetteer's: 核实 = position checked in the source, 推测 = inferred. The English names are our own functional names, not historical ones. Gate names: the film texts (BS_EN) call 水西门 the West Gate and 挹江门 the river gate; the plan's North Gate to the river is 挹江门 (it stands at the north-west corner of the wall, not in the north: the gates in the north wall are labelled in pinyin, mid view only).",
 "frame": "scene metres; x east, z south (as places.json); the label is drawn at the ground point (x, z)",
 "views": {
  "home": "camera distance >= 7000 m (cams.json home / home_v)",
  "mid": "1500 m <= camera distance < 7000 m",
  "close": "camera distance < 1500 m (the 300 m and 1,500 m South Gate stills)"
 },
 "fields": {
  "id": "stable key",
  "ref": "places.json id of the point",
  "zh": "name as in places.json (Simplified)",
  "zh_hant": "the same in Traditional",
  "en": "the functional English name",
  "kind": "places.json kind",
  "size": "L (regions: river, mountain, heights) / M (gates and districts) / S (small): font size step",
  "prio": "1 = always drawn when the camera distance is in dist_m (drop marks before these); 2 = drop when it would overlap a prio-1 label or a mark; 3 = drop first",
  "views": "names of the views that show it (home, mid, close; see views above)",
  "dist_m": "[min, max) camera distance in metres at which it is drawn (the numeric form of views)",
  "side": "preferred side of the label from its point: above | below | left | right (a hint: the layer may flip it to avoid a mark)",
  "x": "scene x (m)",
  "z": "scene z (m)",
  "status": "核实 / 推测 of the position",
  "src": "where the position comes from",
  "note": "what it is"
 },
